<title>USA: Norfolk wants Conrail/CSX amendment nixed.</title>
<headline>Norfolk wants Conrail/CSX amendment nixed.</headline>
<dateline>NORFOLK, Va. 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norfolk Southern Corp said that it has asked the Surface Transportation Board (STB) to rule that a December 18 amendment to the merger agreement between CSX Corp and Conrail Inc constitutes unlawful control by one railroad over another.</p>
<p>The amendment prohibits Conrail, without CSX's consent, from entering into or discussing a merger agreement with any other company until 1999, even if Conrail shareholders or the STB disapprove of the proposed CSX merger.</p>
<p>Norfolk released its statement after business hours Friday.</p>
</text>
